<title>USA: Yellow Corp cuts 102 jobs.</title>
<headline>Yellow Corp cuts 102 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>OVERLAND PARK, Kan 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yellow Corp said Friday that 102 positions were cut from its Yellow Freight System unit as part of a previously announced restructuring.</p>
<p>In addition, 131 of 153 eligible employees have elected to accept early retirement packages, the company said.</p>
<p>During the 1997 first half, an additional 65 to 70 positions will be eliminated through normal attrition, it said.  </p>
<p>The company repeated that it will take an unspecified special charge against fourth quarter earnings for employee severance and retirement packages, as well as the write-down of certain assets and other restructuring-related expenses.</p>
<p>Fourth quarter and full year 1996 financial results will be announced in about two weeks.</p>
<p>Shares of Yellow, which employs about 24,000 people, were unchanged at 16-1/2.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
